      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Adapted from Murray et al.: triethanolamine (0.5 cm3 of a 1.0 M MeOH solution, 0.5 mmol) was added to Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (0.226 g, 0.5 mmol) in MeOH/CH2Cl2 (1:1 v/v, 25 cm3). NEt3 (0.14 cm3, 1.0 mmol) was added and the solution stirred for 10 min. A white precipitate was removed by filtration; colourless plates of 3 crystallised by slow evaporation over 2 d (35% yield). Alternatively, Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (0.226 g, 0.5 mmol), triethanolamine (0.5 cm3 of 1.0 M MeOH, 0.5 mmol), NEt3 (0.14 cm3, 1.0 mmol) and MeOH (8 cm3) were sealed in a Teflon-lined bomb and heated at 130 °C for 24 h; after slow cooling, large colourless crystals were isolated in ca. 90% yield. 3 can also be prepared without NEt3 (yield ca. 30%).",
